  "base_commit": "9960fa7ad3fa9dd57681e29b69f8f33900d2f6b6",
  "scope": "Slot1 and Slot3 reel layout, touch-stop handling, result matching and payout state readability.",
  "changes": [
    "Slot1: model three 21-symbol reel strips instead of one strip plus padding, remove the local SlotReels shadow and use the real scene members in SlotReels_CheckStopped.",
    "Slot1: name reel scroll, spin-sound handle, state, payout multiplier, symbol index, spinning flags, stopped count, speed-table offset, matched symbol, match flag, wild count and state timer; use native result/scroll/index fields in Render.",
    "Slot3: name reel period, difficulty, spin-sound handle, payout remaining, next win symbol, stopped count, state timer and direction array; model the three spinning command flags previously declared as padding.",
    "Slot3: correct mLineActive to mReelStopped: these bytes mark completed stops and captured results, not bets on pay lines.",
    "Slot3: rewrite the touch/reel state with readable variables, native scalar accesses and explicit boundary-stop logic, removing redundant 64-bit casts; retain the measured indexed address construction.",
    "Slot3: use native members in states 0, 2, 3/4 and 6; remove the SlotGrid include and use the scene reel/result arrays; name columns, symbols, payout and score. Clarify ReelDigits cursors."
  ],
  "evidence": {
    "slot1_layout": "InitResources copies three 0x15-byte strips at +0x46c0, +0x46d5 and +0x46ea. Behavior advances +0x46ff indices modulo 21 and decrements +0x46a4 Fix12 scroll by a speed-table entry. Touch clears +0x4702 and increments +0x4705. CheckStopped treats symbol 5 as a wildcard and records its count at +0x470b; matched symbol +0x4709 selects the payout table used with the bet multiplier.",
    "slot3_stop_flags": "StartRound sets +0x502b[3] to 1 and +0x502e[3] to 0. State1 clears the first flags on touch, continues movement to a symbol boundary, captures result symbols and sets the corresponding +0x502e flag to 1. Render tests those completed-stop flags. This contradicts the former pay-line-bet label.",
    "slot3_controls": "StartRound computes +0x4ff0 as stripLength*80<<12. State1 subtracts scroll when +0x5040[i] is 1, otherwise adds; it selects the speed-table row by +0x503d, incremented on each completed stop. State2 seeds +0x5014 with the award, and state3 decrements it while adding credits. +0x503c replaces the displayed win symbol after the marker scroll. +0x5004 selects strip length and directions and increases after a win while below 5; it is initially copied from mLevel, so this report does not claim an unconditional 0..5 range.",
    "ownership": "Queue snapshot build/scene-physics17-queue.json at 630fe3c1bcb91e1d3e26ad2a74d85e4d1e5c4492: no active matching class/file resources and no active ov006 range overlaps 0x0210a8c0..0x0210d740.",
    "runtime_validation": "No new emulator run: names follow explicit initialization, arithmetic, touch writes, result capture and credit updates. No unobserved gameplay behavior is asserted.",
    "retained_constraints": [
      "Fully native Slot3_State1 indexed access grew its body from 664 to 672 bytes. Retaining integer-cast address construction for the stopped flags, scroll pointer and direction restores exact output; the 64-bit casts were unnecessary and removed.",
      "A native mStripLength read in Slot3_ReelDigits grew its body from 136 to 144 bytes. Keep the strided byte cursors and raw strip-length access, now with meaningful local names.",
      "Deleting the zero-valued pointer expression at the end of the Slot3_State2 column loop grew its body from 440 to 472 bytes. Retain it with an explicit matching note.",
      "Preserve the previously measured Slot1 InitResources strip-fill cursor and Behavior case7 strided cursor, the Slot3 Render address constraints, the state pragmas, PMF constants and factory construction sequences.",
      "Unknown fields and embedded object identities remain explicit; no complete-scene reconstruction or original source-name claim."
    ]
  },
